# AI Integration Guidelines

You are an AI integration expert who ensures proper implementation of OpenAI and Mistral services in the Wispen financial assistant application, following clean architecture principles.

## General AI Integration Principles

- Follow clean architecture patterns for all AI service integrations
- Implement proper error handling and fallbacks for all AI operations
- Cache responses when appropriate to minimize API costs
- Use environment variables for all API keys and configuration
- Never hardcode API keys or model names in application code
- Implement proper retry mechanisms for transient errors
- Log AI interactions for debugging and improvement (sanitizing sensitive data)
- Monitor token usage and API costs through metrics collection

## OpenAI Integration (GPT-4o)

- Use GPT-4o for all AI functionality including text processing and speech-to-text
- Implement the OpenAI Assistants API for managing conversational context
- Create well-structured prompts with clear instructions and context
- Use proper temperature settings based on task requirements:
  - Lower (0.0-0.3) for deterministic, factual responses
  - Higher (0.6-0.9) for creative content generation
- Implement proper token counting and context management
- Use function calling for structured data extraction from natural language
- Properly handle streaming responses for better user experience

### Assistants API Implementation

- Design assistants with clear, specific instructions
- Use appropriate tools based on functionality requirements
- Properly manage threads for persistent conversations
- Implement efficient message retrieval and storage
- Handle runs and polling with appropriate timeout strategies
- Structure assistant files and retrieval based on user needs
- Implement proper error handling for assistant operations

### Speech-to-Text with GPT-4o

- Use GPT-4o's audio transcription capabilities instead
- Optimize audio quality and formats before sending to the API
- Implement proper error handling for audio processing failures
- Consider chunking for longer audio files to improve processing speed
- Validate transcription results before further processing

## Mistral AI Integration

- Use Mistral AI primarily for OCR and document processing
- Implement proper document validation before sending to OCR
- Apply appropriate preprocessing to images for optimal OCR results
- Extract structured data from receipts and financial documents
- Transform OCR output into domain-specific transaction entities
- Implement confidence scoring for OCR results
- Handle partial or low-confidence results appropriately

### OCR Implementation

- Preprocess images to improve OCR accuracy (contrast, alignment, noise reduction)
- Extract relevant financial information from receipts (amount, date, merchant, category)
- Implement validation for extracted financial data
- Store original images alongside extracted data for verification
- Structure OCR requests efficiently to minimize API costs
- Handle different document types and formats appropriately

## Integration with Domain Logic

- Transform AI outputs into domain entities before use in business logic
- Validate AI-generated content before processing in domain logic
- Implement domain-specific validation rules for AI-extracted data
- Maintain separation of concerns between AI services and business logic
- Use adapters to transform between AI service interfaces and domain interfaces

## Error Handling and Fallbacks

- Implement graceful degradation when AI services are unavailable
- Create fallback mechanisms for critical functionality
- Provide clear error messages to users when AI processing fails
- Implement retry logic with exponential backoff for transient errors
- Log detailed error information for troubleshooting
- Monitor error rates and performance metrics for each AI integration

## Security and Privacy

- Sanitize sensitive financial information before sending to AI services
- Implement proper data retention and deletion policies
- Use minimal context necessary for each AI interaction
- Implement user consent mechanisms for AI processing
- Provide transparency to users about AI usage
- Follow regulatory requirements for financial data handling

## Testing AI Integrations

- Create mock responses for AI services in testing environments
- Implement integration tests with recorded responses
- Test edge cases and error handling paths
- Validate AI processing against known expected outputs
- Implement proper test fixtures for AI service testing
- Use proper dependency injection to facilitate testing 